nhealthy in staging. We rolled checkout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 18115, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_015N6QDGPUFvAjfN14qn2Aar", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18115, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015N6QDGPUFvAjfN14qn2Aar", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 21683, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001**, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Cause:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. It's now running in all three regions.\n- **Result:** After the rollback the service passes health checks and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the next step: finding out why v2.3.1 failed before anyone redeploys it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019wJwaZ1JvVp2cJ9VjPUep6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name"